on talks]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136176184.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/eisenkot-bags-1st-coalition-pact-in-govt-formation-talks/articleshow/136176184.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/eisenkot-bags-1st-coalition-pact-in-govt-formation-talks/articleshow/136176184.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T07:53:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Bloomberg</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136176477,imgsize-58502.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Trouble for Netanyahu? Israeli judges question key charges in corruption trial]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136175855.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/netanyahus-corruption-trial-at-a-turning-point-israeli-judges-question-key-charges-against-pm/articleshow/136175855.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/netanyahus-corruption-trial-at-a-turning-point-israeli-judges-question-key-charges-against-pm/articleshow/136175855.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T07:44:35+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Prisha Patnaik</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136176397,imgsize-63010.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Black nurses faced alleged racial abuse at Vermont home; Elderwood agrees to $450,000 settlement]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136155710.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The settlement of $450,000 addresses allegations of racial harassment faced by Black nurses during the COVID-19 pandemic. Employees reported incidents involving racial slurs and threats from residents at Elderwood at Burlington. The lawsuit was filed by the EEOC, claiming the operators failed to protect their employees from harassment. New measures will be introduced, including updated anti-discrimination policies and training programs for staff.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/black-nurses-left-their-homes-and-families-to-help-a-vermont-nursing-home-during-the-pandemic-four-years-after-a-federal-lawsuit-was-filed-over-alleged-racial-harassment-elderwood-agrees-to-a-450000-settlement/articleshow/136155710.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/black-nurses-left-their-homes-and-families-to-help-a-vermont-nursing-home-during-the-pandemic-four-years-after-a-federal-lawsuit-was-filed-over-alleged-racial-harassment-elderwood-agrees-to-a-450000-settlement/articleshow/136155710.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T08:01:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136155854,imgsize-1779438.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Elise Stefanik family’s DC home sells for $2.9m cash after failing to fetch $1.99m, flagged as unusual]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136171929.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a notable real estate transaction, a Washington home belonging to US Congresswoman Elise Stefanik's family was sold for a substantial $2.9 million in June. This sale came after an earlier unsuccessful attempt to sell at $1.99 million. City tax officials raised eyebrows regarding the deal's unusual price point. The buyer, AFS Real Estate Holdings, remains shrouded in mystery regarding its ownership.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-washington-home-owned-by-us-congresswoman-elise-stefaniks-family-failed-to-sell-at-1-99-million-then-fetched-2-9-million-in-cash-city-records-now-flag-the-transaction-as-unusual/articleshow/136171929.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-washington-home-owned-by-us-congresswoman-elise-stefaniks-family-failed-to-sell-at-1-99-million-then-fetched-2-9-million-in-cash-city-records-now-flag-the-transaction-as-unusual/articleshow/136171929.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T02:04:16+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136172299,imgsize-1186721.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Lululemon founder Chip Wilson says Canadian women aren't having as many babies as men want; some men may need to import brides from Thailand]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136172138.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/lululemon-founder-chip-wilson-says-canadian-women-arent-having-as-many-babies-as-men-want-some-men-may-need-to-import-brides-from-thailand/articleshow/136172138.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/lululemon-founder-chip-wilson-says-canadian-women-arent-having-as-many-babies-as-men-want-some-men-may-need-to-import-brides-from-thailand/articleshow/136172138.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T01:31:25+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136172168,imgsize-49148.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Bournemouth residents oppose two new padel courts, citing noise and swearing from existing courts]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136171836.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Residents near West Hants Club are voicing opposition to proposed new padel courts due to existing noise issues. They report constant disturbances from shouts and sounds that disrupt their daily lives and enjoyment of outdoor spaces. Complaints have been made to BCP Council regarding noise levels and offensive language from players. The club claims it operates responsibly, with measures to manage noise and ensure member behavior.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/residents-living-near-1-million-homes-in-bournemouth-say-a-private-tennis-clubs-padel-courts-bring-constant-noise-and-swearing-they-are-fighting-a-proposal-for-two-more-floodlit-courts-close-to-gardens/articleshow/136171836.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/residents-living-near-1-million-homes-in-bournemouth-say-a-private-tennis-clubs-padel-courts-bring-constant-noise-and-swearing-they-are-fighting-a-proposal-for-two-more-floodlit-courts-close-to-gardens/articleshow/136171836.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T01:00:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136171911,imgsize-2211641.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Egypt highway inferno kills 30 after fuel tanker overturns]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136171820.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A harrowing event unfolded in Giza's Al-Warraq district when a vehicle turned over and burst into flames. Tragically, over 30 individuals perished, while another 21 suffered injuries. Emergency services quickly arrived at the scene to extinguish the blaze and offer medical assistance. The incident took place on a major ring road in Greater Cairo, raising renewed concerns about the pressing issues of road safety in Egypt.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/30-killed-15-injured-in-deadly-blaze-on-cairo-ring-road-after-fuel-vehicle-overturns/articleshow/136171820.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/30-killed-15-injured-in-deadly-blaze-on-cairo-ring-road-after-fuel-vehicle-overturns/articleshow/136171820.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T00:56:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136171841,imgsize-238834.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Chinese scientist, Arizona State University assistant professor, says he does not know why he was arrested by ICE: 'I still have nightmares']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136171792.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/chinese-scientist-arizona-state-university-assistant-professor-says-he-does-not-know-why-he-was-arrested-by-ice-i-still-have-nightmares/articleshow/136171792.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/chinese-scientist-arizona-state-university-assistant-professor-says-he-does-not-know-why-he-was-arrested-by-ice-i-still-have-nightmares/articleshow/136171792.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T00:53:48+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136171828,imgsize-140096.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Michigan widow's $78m truck crash award cut by $24m as court orders retrial on $19m claim]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136171612.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Michigan appeals court overturned a $24 million award for pre-impact fright in a wrongful death case. The court ruled that state law does not allow compensation for fear experienced before injury. A new trial has been ordered for the $19 million awarded for conscious pain and suffering. The trial originally awarded over $78 million for the negligence of an 18-wheel lorry driver.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-michigan-widow-once-won-more-than-78-million-after-a-truck-crash-killed-her-husband-and-son-an-appeals-court-has-now-thrown-out-24-million-for-their-pre-impact-fear-and-ordered-a-retrial-on-19-million/articleshow/136171612.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-michigan-widow-once-won-more-than-78-million-after-a-truck-crash-killed-her-husband-and-son-an-appeals-court-has-now-thrown-out-24-million-for-their-pre-impact-fear-and-ordered-a-retrial-on-19-million/articleshow/136171612.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T00:53:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136171823,imgsize-1842179.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Alberta family donates 160 acres of native prairie for conservation while allowing cattle grazing]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136171418.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A remarkable commitment to conservation has been made by a ranching family in southern Alberta, who have donated 160 acres of untouched prairie land for long-term protection. This initiative allows cattle grazing to persist while maintaining the delicate balance of the native grassland ecosystem. For nearly a century, the Coppieters family has managed this land, protecting its agricultural history.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-1925-a-canadian-family-began-farming-in-southern-alberta-101-years-later-descendants-have-donated-160-acres-of-native-grassland-that-will-remain-protected-while-ranchers-continue-grazing-cattle/articleshow/136171418.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-1925-a-canadian-family-began-farming-in-southern-alberta-101-years-later-descendants-have-donated-160-acres-of-native-grassland-that-will-remain-protected-while-ranchers-continue-grazing-cattle/articleshow/136171418.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T00:29:57+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136171601,imgsize-2178564.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Florida employer to pay $112,500 after accounting clerk's cancer-related dismissal claim]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136153490.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[After undergoing cancer surgery, a Florida employee sought temporary accommodations, only to be let go by Schumacher Auto Group. The US Equal Employment Opportunity Commission has since accused the company of discrimination under the Americans with Disabilities Act. As part of a settlement, Schumacher will pay $112,500 in damages and revise their disability policies.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2024-a-florida-accounting-clerk-allegedly-lost-her-job-while-recovering-from-cancer-surgery-and-seeking-temporary-work-restrictions-two-years-later-her-employer-agrees-to-pay-her-112500/articleshow/136153490.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2024-a-florida-accounting-clerk-allegedly-lost-her-job-while-recovering-from-cancer-surgery-and-seeking-temporary-work-restrictions-two-years-later-her-employer-agrees-to-pay-her-112500/articleshow/136153490.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T05:57:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136153594,imgsize-96294.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[New homes now cost $40K less than resale in the US]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136155429.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Current housing data shows a significant price gap between newly built homes and existing properties. Builders are implementing price cuts and incentives to attract buyers amid weaker demand. A median family finds new homes slightly more affordable than existing ones, despite high mortgage rates. Certain markets still experience severe housing cost burdens, requiring a significant portion of income for mortgage payments.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/a-typical-new-home-in-the-us-now-sells-for-393300-almost-40000-less-than-an-existing-home-the-widest-gap-on-record-as-43-of-builders-cut-prices-last-month-to-lure-more-buyers/articleshow/136155429.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/a-typical-new-home-in-the-us-now-sells-for-393300-almost-40000-less-than-an-existing-home-the-widest-gap-on-record-as-43-of-builders-cut-prices-last-month-to-lure-more-buyers/articleshow/136155429.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T05:53:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136155842,imgsize-268172.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Neighbour blocks couple's waterfront access, court upholds $64,061 legal fee award]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136152015.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Minnesota couple sued their neighbour after he put up a sign claiming they had no harbour access and parked his boat along their waterfront, disrupting their attempts to sell two properties. An appeals court ruled that their property titles expressly granted water access, upheld findings of slander of title and nuisance, and confirmed a $64,061 attorney-fee award.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-minnesota-couple-put-two-waterfront-lots-up-for-sale-but-their-neighbour-posted-a-sign-denying-harbour-access-and-moored-his-boat-in-front-a-november-23-appeals-ruling-upheld-64061-in-legal-fees/articleshow/136152015.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-minnesota-couple-put-two-waterfront-lots-up-for-sale-but-their-neighbour-posted-a-sign-denying-harbour-access-and-moored-his-boat-in-front-a-november-23-appeals-ruling-upheld-64061-in-legal-fees/articleshow/136152015.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T04:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136152387,imgsize-216028.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Florida jury awards $6M to family of man who died during elective neck surgery]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136155315.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/florida-jury-awarded-6-million-to-the-wife-and-two-daughters-of-carlos-chalbaud-who-died-on-the-operating-table-during-elective-neck-surgery-at-holy-cross-hospital-without-clearance-from-a-cardiologist/articleshow/136155315.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/florida-jury-awarded-6-million-to-the-wife-and-two-daughters-of-carlos-chalbaud-who-died-on-the-operating-table-during-elective-neck-surgery-at-holy-cross-hospital-without-clearance-from-a-cardiologist/articleshow/136155315.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T04:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136155360,imgsize-802985.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Colorado court upholds injunction over ranch road used by a family since 1958]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136152835.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Colorado ranching family used a road for livestock since 1958 but lost access rights in court. The new owners, Camilletti Ranch Properties LLC, challenged their claim to a prescriptive easement. The court ruled that the family's use was permitted by previous owners during part of the statutory period. The Colorado Court of Appeals affirmed this decision on November 12, 2026.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-colorado-ranching-familys-use-of-a-three-mile-road-across-neighbouring-land-dates-back-to-1958-but-new-owners-challenged-their-access-a-november-12-ruling-upheld-a-permanent-injunction/articleshow/136152835.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-colorado-ranching-familys-use-of-a-three-mile-road-across-neighbouring-land-dates-back-to-1958-but-new-owners-challenged-their-access-a-november-12-ruling-upheld-a-permanent-injunction/articleshow/136152835.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T03:52:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https